From f8bc968034e4d95eb2afe5b817c762f7eab4188a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: testuser <mainta@example.test>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:05:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/11] build(cli): compile telemetry out unless the build opts
 in

The CLI bundle (bun.mts) and the compiled binaries (script/build.ts)
inline telemetry settings from the build shell as Bun defines:
OpenTelemetry export and its endpoint and headers, trace content
recording, the PostHog key that drives feature-flag polling against
data.cline.bot, and the error-service key. Defines replace the
process.env reads at compile time, so a shipped binary cannot be
reconfigured at runtime; the only runtime escape was IS_TEST/E2E_TEST.
Any from-source build also inherited whatever OTEL_* values its shell
happened to carry.

Add script/telemetry-defines.ts with a build telemetry mode:

- off (default): every telemetry variable inlines a disabled value
  whatever the build shell contains: OTEL_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=false,
  exporters none, CLINE_TRACE_RECORD_CONTENT=false, sample percent 0,
  and empty endpoint, headers, PostHog and error-service keys. With an
  empty key the CLI uses NoOpFeatureFlagsProvider, so feature flags are
  never polled, without IS_TEST. bun.mts also stops inlining OTEL_*
  through Bun's env option.
- on: the previous inline-from-environment behavior, unchanged.
  Selected with --telemetry=on or CLINE_BUILD_TELEMETRY=on; the
  cli-publish workflow now sets CLINE_BUILD_TELEMETRY=on on every step
  that injects telemetry secrets, so release builds are unchanged.

An off build asserts after compiling that no telemetry endpoint,
header or key value from the build shell appears in the binary, and
fails the build otherwise.

Tests: 9 new tests for mode resolution, off/on defines, the runtime
effect on the shared telemetry config, and the leak check; 1 guard
test that the CLI feature-flag service stays on the no-op provider
without IS_TEST when the key is empty.
